app/test-results/
app/playwright-report/
.unlighthouse/
output/
*.png
# ...but EVERY PWA / apple-touch / startup / screenshot PNG in public/ MUST
# deploy (Netlify builds from git, so blanket-ignoring these 404s the live
# manifest icons, iOS startup images, and install-dialog screenshots).
# The negation below used to be `!app/public/*.png`, which only covers the top
# level — its own comment claimed directory-level coverage it did not have.
# Verified with git check-ignore: app/public/test.png was negated, while
# app/public/assets/test.png, app/public/assets/social/test.png and
# app/public/examples/audit/test.png were all ignored by `*.png` above. The 15
# nested PNGs tracked today survive only because they predate the rule; a new
# one would have gone missing silently — present locally, 404 in production,
# since Netlify builds from git. `**/` matches zero or more directories, so this
# single line covers both the top level and any depth beneath it.
!app/public/**/*.png
!app/public/brand-kit/
!app/public/brand-kit/**
*.bak
docs/
firebase-debug.log
.claude/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
!/package-lock.json
!app/package-lock.json
dist/
dist-*/

# --- secrets & local cruft (added during 2026-06-30 consolidation) ---
.env
*.env
.env.*
app/.env
tmp/
backup/
deploy-*.zip
*.zip
!app/public/brand-kit/assets/downloads/little-fight-nyc-brand-kit.zip
_qa/
